1
00:00:00,467 --> 00:00:01,692
What does it take...

2
00:00:01,746 --> 00:00:02,800
(Truly falling for someone.)

3
00:00:02,806 --> 00:00:03,566
...to truly fall for someone?

4
00:00:03,633 --> 00:00:06,167
So, this friend of yours
hated him at first,

5
00:00:06,267 --> 00:00:08,533
but slowly started to like him, right?

6
00:00:08,633 --> 00:00:13,133
Does "liking" someone mean
wanting to be by their side forever?

7
00:00:13,467 --> 00:00:16,367
Maybe I can only be my true self
when I'm with Na-chan.

8
00:00:17,467 --> 00:00:19,567
That's a secret just between you and me.

9
00:00:20,200 --> 00:00:21,200
It's a promise.

10
00:00:22,100 --> 00:00:23,267
I understand.

11
00:00:30,700 --> 00:00:33,067
"Your Summer, My Storm"
(Episode 5)

12
00:00:41,800 --> 00:00:43,900
All right, let's begin
today's cooking class.

13
00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:45,367
- Okay.
- Looking forward to it.

14
00:00:45,467 --> 00:00:46,567
What are we making today?

15
00:00:46,667 --> 00:00:47,667
I can't wait.

16
00:00:47,700 --> 00:00:48,567
Here.

17
00:00:48,667 --> 00:00:50,067
Why do I have to join too?

18
00:00:50,167 --> 00:00:52,633
A bet is a bet, so stop complaining.

19
00:00:53,933 --> 00:00:54,600
No way.

20
00:00:54,700 --> 00:00:55,833
Come on, please.

21
00:00:56,333 --> 00:00:58,209
(1 hour ago)
I am not going to be my mom's student.

22
00:00:58,233 --> 00:01:01,167
I heard everyone else there
is older than me.

23
00:01:01,800 --> 00:01:03,943
Aren't you good at handling
this kind of stuff, So-chan?

24
00:01:03,967 --> 00:01:06,467
At least come with me for the first class.

25
00:01:06,967 --> 00:01:07,967
Please?

26
00:01:09,167 --> 00:01:10,167
Good luck with that.

27
00:01:10,267 --> 00:01:12,100
Na-chan.

28
00:01:13,067 --> 00:01:13,867
You're so annoying.

29
00:01:13,967 --> 00:01:14,967
How about this...

30
00:01:16,533 --> 00:01:17,733
Let's settle this with a game.

31
00:01:19,333 --> 00:01:21,067
Ready... go!

32
00:01:29,067 --> 00:01:30,500
Yes, I win!

33
00:01:30,600 --> 00:01:31,767
Damn it, I lost.

34
00:01:31,867 --> 00:01:33,533
Why did I even agree to play?

35
00:01:33,633 --> 00:01:35,300
Just accept your fate.

36
00:01:36,567 --> 00:01:39,900
We have two new students joining us today.

37
00:01:40,000 --> 00:01:41,367
This is Kobayakawa Sota-san.

38
00:01:41,467 --> 00:01:43,176
- The pleasure is mine.
- Looking forward to it.

39
00:01:43,200 --> 00:01:44,467
You look great in that apron.

40
00:01:44,567 --> 00:01:46,600
We're the boys' team. Nice to meet you all.

41
00:01:46,700 --> 00:01:48,767
And this is my son, Natsuki.

42
00:01:48,867 --> 00:01:50,800
He might be a bit of a handful.

43
00:01:50,900 --> 00:01:53,167
Please feel free to put him to work.

44
00:01:53,267 --> 00:01:54,000
Nice to meet you.

45
00:01:54,100 --> 00:01:56,309
I never thought the day would come
when I'd get to cook with Natsuki.

46
00:01:56,333 --> 00:01:58,967
- Right?
- As a fan, I'm absolutely thrilled.

47
00:01:59,067 --> 00:02:01,133
Men who can cook are very popular.

48
00:02:01,233 --> 00:02:03,100
- Oh, stop it.
- So that's what you're after.

49
00:02:03,200 --> 00:02:04,943
- Who would've thought?
- That's not it at all.

50
00:02:04,967 --> 00:02:07,309
I'm just giving some advice
to a young man struggling with love.

51
00:02:07,333 --> 00:02:10,200
Everyone, let's wrap
up the chatting for now.

52
00:02:10,300 --> 00:02:11,943
Yanagi-san, this is your
fault. You got us scolded.

53
00:02:11,967 --> 00:02:13,100
Huh? Is it my fault?

54
00:02:13,200 --> 00:02:15,167
Today, we'll be using olive oil

55
00:02:15,267 --> 00:02:17,900
to make two types of salads, gazpacho,

56
00:02:18,000 --> 00:02:19,867
and pasta.

57
00:02:19,967 --> 00:02:22,000
For the ingredients, we have...

58
00:02:22,100 --> 00:02:23,867
(Sanada Ryunken)
Welcome!

59
00:02:24,067 --> 00:02:25,067
Ah!

60
00:02:25,867 --> 00:02:26,567
Why are you yelling all of a sudden?

61
00:02:26,667 --> 00:02:29,000
It seems Natsuki has a crush on someone.

62
00:02:29,800 --> 00:02:30,800
Huh?

63
00:02:31,367 --> 00:02:32,133
Who is it?

64
00:02:32,233 --> 00:02:34,300
No, I don't know who it is either.

65
00:02:34,400 --> 00:02:35,400
What the heck...

66
00:02:35,433 --> 00:02:39,233
But he came to me for relationship advice
under the guise of "asking for a friend."

67
00:02:39,333 --> 00:02:40,576
That's definitely about himself, right?

68
00:02:40,600 --> 00:02:41,600
- Right?
- Yeah.

69
00:02:41,633 --> 00:02:43,900
By the way, when did this start?

70
00:02:44,000 --> 00:02:48,100
Well, it sounds like he's
trying to steal someone's girl.

71
00:02:48,200 --> 00:02:49,200
What?

72
00:02:49,333 --> 00:02:50,533
Is Natsuki having an affair?

73
00:02:50,633 --> 00:02:53,133
No, it doesn't seem like that either.

74
00:02:54,067 --> 00:02:56,707
It sounds like he fell for the
girlfriend of someone close to him.

75
00:02:56,733 --> 00:02:57,733
Are you serious?

76
00:02:59,067 --> 00:03:02,867
But I don't think he specifically
said it was someone close to him...

77
00:03:03,933 --> 00:03:05,000
What was it again?

78
00:03:05,467 --> 00:03:06,467
A lover?

79
00:03:06,933 --> 00:03:09,433
Wow.

80
00:03:09,533 --> 00:03:10,700
That's amazing...

81
00:03:10,800 --> 00:03:13,133
Sota-san, you're incredible.

82
00:03:13,233 --> 00:03:14,233
Thank you.

83
00:03:14,533 --> 00:03:18,800
Your willingness to challenge yourself
with anything is a great trait to have.

84
00:03:18,900 --> 00:03:20,467
He already likes cooking, doesn't he?

85
00:03:20,567 --> 00:03:22,309
You can tell a lot about a person's
attitude from just one thing.

86
00:03:22,333 --> 00:03:23,833
Natsuki, you should learn from him.

87
00:03:23,933 --> 00:03:24,933
Ouch!

88
00:03:25,000 --> 00:03:26,867
Stop exaggerating and get to work.

89
00:03:26,967 --> 00:03:28,687
Here, take the cucumber and start chopping.

90
00:03:36,133 --> 00:03:37,200
What's wrong?

91
00:03:37,733 --> 00:03:39,100
Your socks.

92
00:03:39,600 --> 00:03:40,600
Huh?

93
00:03:41,400 --> 00:03:42,600
Ah, huh?

94
00:03:42,867 --> 00:03:45,600
How did that happen? I
swear I put on a matching pair.

95
00:03:45,967 --> 00:03:48,000
So-chan surprisingly has a clumsy side too.

96
00:03:48,100 --> 00:03:50,067
That's not true at all.

97
00:03:50,633 --> 00:03:53,233
Didn't you wear your T-shirt
inside out last time too?

98
00:03:53,833 --> 00:03:57,267
That's because it's hard
to tell with a white T-shirt.

99
00:03:57,767 --> 00:03:58,767
Is that so?

100
00:03:59,167 --> 00:04:00,200
I'm serious!

101
00:04:07,967 --> 00:04:09,733
Mmm, delicious.

102
00:04:09,833 --> 00:04:11,500
That's the cucumber I chopped, you know.

103
00:04:12,167 --> 00:04:13,667
Chopping the cucumber is all you did.

104
00:04:13,967 --> 00:04:17,767
Well, if I hurt my hand, it
would affect my studies.

105
00:04:17,967 --> 00:04:19,433
That's true.

106
00:04:20,800 --> 00:04:22,000
Do you want some too, Na-chan?

107
00:04:22,400 --> 00:04:23,400
- Here.
- Huh?

108
00:04:23,600 --> 00:04:24,667
Open wide.

109
00:04:30,967 --> 00:04:31,467
It's good.

110
00:04:31,567 --> 00:04:33,633
I was going to feed it to you.

111
00:04:33,733 --> 00:04:35,176
- No thanks.
- Why are you being so shy?

112
00:04:35,200 --> 00:04:36,933
They seem to be having a lot of fun.

113
00:04:37,033 --> 00:04:40,100
Watching handsome guys
fool around is so therapeutic.

114
00:04:40,200 --> 00:04:42,233
It's a real feast for the eyes.

115
00:04:42,333 --> 00:04:43,633
It's not yours.

116
00:04:43,733 --> 00:04:45,167
Here, Yui, enjoy.

117
00:04:45,267 --> 00:04:47,533
Natsuki in love, huh...

118
00:04:47,967 --> 00:04:49,433
Does Rio-san know about this?

119
00:04:49,533 --> 00:04:50,833
Is Rio still in Okinawa?

120
00:04:50,933 --> 00:04:51,500
Yeah.

121
00:04:51,800 --> 00:04:52,267
Ah.

122
00:04:52,367 --> 00:04:53,367
Hmm?

123
00:04:54,400 --> 00:04:55,867
Looks like she'll be back soon.

124
00:04:56,600 --> 00:04:58,400
Let's eat.

125
00:04:58,500 --> 00:04:59,667
Here... enjoy.

126
00:04:59,767 --> 00:05:00,767
Great, isn't it?

127
00:05:01,200 --> 00:05:03,900
Fuku-chan, you didn't even make these.

128
00:05:04,000 --> 00:05:05,067
My bad.

129
00:05:05,167 --> 00:05:07,300
I just came to return the plates.

130
00:05:07,400 --> 00:05:09,267
And you even let me join in.

131
00:05:09,767 --> 00:05:11,367
Your timing is impeccable.

132
00:05:11,667 --> 00:05:14,300
- Delicious.
- He really nailed the timing.

133
00:05:14,400 --> 00:05:18,133
The ratio of guys today... or rather, the
ratio of handsome guys is especially high.

134
00:05:18,233 --> 00:05:19,700
It's quite rare.

135
00:05:19,800 --> 00:05:22,167
To think there are guys in
Towako-san's cooking class.

136
00:05:22,267 --> 00:05:26,833
Yeah, Yanagi-san is the second,
and Sota-san is the third.

137
00:05:27,467 --> 00:05:29,376
Why did you decide to take
cooking classes, Yanagi-san?

138
00:05:29,400 --> 00:05:32,900
I wanted to make better
bento boxes for my grandson.

139
00:05:33,533 --> 00:05:35,543
The kindergarten he goes to
requires them to bring their own lunch.

140
00:05:35,567 --> 00:05:37,367
Wait, you make all of Riku's bento boxes?

141
00:05:37,467 --> 00:05:39,067
Because I'm the only one who can.

142
00:05:39,167 --> 00:05:42,000
His mom is swamped with work
and is incredibly busy every day.

143
00:05:42,100 --> 00:05:44,567
So Yanagi-san makes all of Riku's lunches.

144
00:05:44,667 --> 00:05:48,633
At first, he couldn't even tell the
difference between tamagoyaki and a fried egg.

145
00:05:48,733 --> 00:05:51,009
- He's really improved a lot.
- Please don't bring that up.

146
00:05:51,033 --> 00:05:53,567
No, Yanagi-san is truly amazing.

147
00:05:53,667 --> 00:05:58,367
My dad used to cook for
me when I was little too.

148
00:05:58,467 --> 00:06:01,676
But it was always just rice with pickled
plum, the simplest bento you could imagine.

149
00:06:01,700 --> 00:06:04,700
Looking back on it now,
it's just a funny memory.

150
00:06:05,000 --> 00:06:06,067
By the way, Kaoru-san.

151
00:06:06,167 --> 00:06:10,700
Last time, you went out of your way to teach me
how many slices per loaf to buy at the bakery.

152
00:06:10,800 --> 00:06:12,009
That really helped me out a lot.

153
00:06:12,033 --> 00:06:13,400
You're very welcome.

154
00:06:13,500 --> 00:06:15,600
Did the sandwiches turn out well?

155
00:06:15,700 --> 00:06:18,500
Thanks to you, Riku happily ate them all.

156
00:06:18,600 --> 00:06:20,067
Riku is a lucky boy.

157
00:06:20,167 --> 00:06:24,200
He even told me he wants
a character bento next time.

158
00:06:24,300 --> 00:06:25,133
A character bento?

159
00:06:25,233 --> 00:06:27,467
Yanagi-san, I'm so impressed by you.

160
00:06:29,500 --> 00:06:30,400
Eat up...

161
00:06:30,500 --> 00:06:33,667
- Not again.
- I told you, you didn't make these.

162
00:06:35,633 --> 00:06:38,033
Natsuki, go feed Rock.

163
00:06:38,133 --> 00:06:39,300
Ah, okay.

164
00:06:43,167 --> 00:06:43,967
Careful.

165
00:06:44,067 --> 00:06:45,467
I got this.

166
00:06:46,233 --> 00:06:47,233
Huh?

167
00:06:48,500 --> 00:06:49,500
Ah!

168
00:06:58,100 --> 00:06:59,300
See? I told you to be careful.

169
00:07:02,100 --> 00:07:03,400
I'm home!

170
00:07:04,400 --> 00:07:04,800
Huh?

171
00:07:04,900 --> 00:07:06,867
- Rock!
- Huh?

172
00:07:07,933 --> 00:07:09,133
I'm home!

173
00:07:09,233 --> 00:07:10,467
Welcome back.

174
00:07:10,567 --> 00:07:12,367
Did you say you were coming back today?

175
00:07:12,467 --> 00:07:13,233
Did I not?

176
00:07:13,333 --> 00:07:14,167
I didn't hear anything about it.

177
00:07:14,267 --> 00:07:15,267
Is that so?

178
00:07:15,400 --> 00:07:17,167
Ah, Sota.

179
00:07:18,367 --> 00:07:19,233
I'm back.

180
00:07:19,333 --> 00:07:19,967
Welcome back.

181
00:07:20,067 --> 00:07:20,833
How was Okinawa?

182
00:07:20,933 --> 00:07:22,033
It was amazing.

183
00:07:24,200 --> 00:07:28,200
Ah, you must have caught a cold because you
missed me too much while I was gone, right?

184
00:07:28,300 --> 00:07:29,500
No, I'm fine.

185
00:07:29,600 --> 00:07:30,633
- Really?
- Yeah.

186
00:07:30,733 --> 00:07:31,467
Ah, here's a souvenir.

187
00:07:31,567 --> 00:07:32,700
Thank you.

188
00:07:32,967 --> 00:07:34,033
Natsuki.

189
00:07:34,267 --> 00:07:35,700
Have you been studying hard?

190
00:07:36,000 --> 00:07:36,800
Of course.

191
00:07:36,900 --> 00:07:37,900
Really?

192
00:07:38,267 --> 00:07:41,000
At this rate, his next mock
exam scores should improve a lot.

193
00:07:41,100 --> 00:07:42,833
That's pretty impressive.

194
00:07:43,200 --> 00:07:43,900
It's nothing much.

195
00:07:44,000 --> 00:07:45,133
That's Sota for you.

196
00:07:45,367 --> 00:07:46,233
I'm the impressive one here, right?

197
00:07:46,333 --> 00:07:47,567
- Um, Rio.
- Hmm?

198
00:07:47,667 --> 00:07:49,700
Did you buy the Okinawan salt?

199
00:07:49,967 --> 00:07:51,200
- Ah...
- Huh?

200
00:07:51,300 --> 00:07:52,567
Did you forget?

201
00:07:52,667 --> 00:07:54,533
I reminded you so many times.

202
00:07:54,633 --> 00:07:55,767
You can just buy it online.

203
00:07:55,867 --> 00:07:57,767
Then it wouldn't be a souvenir.

204
00:07:57,867 --> 00:07:59,100
Isn't that right, Sota-san?

205
00:07:59,200 --> 00:08:00,200
Exactly.

206
00:08:00,267 --> 00:08:00,667
- Yeah.
- Huh?

207
00:08:00,767 --> 00:08:01,367
Oh, come on.

208
00:08:01,467 --> 00:08:04,100
Did my mom somehow rope you in
while I was away?

209
00:08:04,200 --> 00:08:06,867
He even came to the cooking class today.

210
00:08:06,967 --> 00:08:07,967
Right?

211
00:08:08,000 --> 00:08:09,600
- Wait, Sota did?
- So she's back...

212
00:08:13,467 --> 00:08:14,733
Okay.

213
00:08:18,767 --> 00:08:19,833
(So close!)

214
00:08:20,667 --> 00:08:22,200
(That's it.)

215
00:08:31,533 --> 00:08:32,967
(Truly falling for someone.)

216
00:08:33,047 --> 00:08:35,713
What does it take
to truly fall for someone?

217
00:08:38,667 --> 00:08:40,133
Natsuki.

218
00:08:41,067 --> 00:08:42,733
- A souvenir.
- A souvenir?

219
00:08:42,833 --> 00:08:43,833
Which one do you like?

220
00:08:45,267 --> 00:08:47,100
Hmm... This one.

221
00:08:47,200 --> 00:08:49,200
I knew you'd pick that one.

222
00:08:49,300 --> 00:08:50,500
I prefer this one too.

223
00:08:50,767 --> 00:08:51,767
Thanks.

224
00:08:52,067 --> 00:08:54,367
After all, we like the same things.

225
00:08:55,200 --> 00:08:56,267
That's not true.

226
00:09:02,367 --> 00:09:03,700
Huh, did you need something?

227
00:09:04,333 --> 00:09:05,333
Not really.

228
00:09:06,633 --> 00:09:07,533
I'm studying here.

229
00:09:07,633 --> 00:09:08,633
Natsuki.

230
00:09:09,033 --> 00:09:10,913
- What?
- I heard you've got a crush on someone?

231
00:09:11,167 --> 00:09:12,167
Huh?

232
00:09:12,233 --> 00:09:13,667
Yui just told me.

233
00:09:13,767 --> 00:09:14,400
Yui-san?

234
00:09:14,500 --> 00:09:15,500
Yeah.

235
00:09:15,533 --> 00:09:16,533
Why?

236
00:09:16,800 --> 00:09:18,433
Didn't you go ask Ryo about it?

237
00:09:18,533 --> 00:09:20,267
Pretending you were asking for a friend.

238
00:09:21,567 --> 00:09:23,333
He saw right through you.

239
00:09:24,333 --> 00:09:25,233
That blabbermouth.

240
00:09:25,333 --> 00:09:26,333
Who is it?

241
00:09:27,833 --> 00:09:28,367
Huh?

242
00:09:28,633 --> 00:09:30,673
And I heard you're stealing
someone else's partner.

243
00:09:31,067 --> 00:09:32,067
What?

244
00:09:36,733 --> 00:09:37,767
Feels so good.

245
00:09:38,333 --> 00:09:39,653
(Hokkaido Hot Spring Inn Special)

246
00:09:40,567 --> 00:09:41,433
What are you looking at?

247
00:09:41,533 --> 00:09:42,300
Huh?

248
00:09:42,400 --> 00:09:43,567
Nothing, it's nothing.

249
00:09:44,000 --> 00:09:44,700
Right?

250
00:09:44,933 --> 00:09:46,133
I wasn't looking at anything.

251
00:09:46,233 --> 00:09:47,333
Isn't that right, Rock?

252
00:09:48,467 --> 00:09:49,133
You smiled.

253
00:09:49,233 --> 00:09:52,467
I can't believe Natsuki actually
has a crush on someone.

254
00:09:52,767 --> 00:09:54,867
I told you it's not like that.

255
00:09:56,367 --> 00:10:00,007
Setting aside whether stealing someone's partner
is right or wrong in the eyes of society...

256
00:10:00,267 --> 00:10:05,186
I'm just glad you finally
found someone you like.

257
00:10:07,267 --> 00:10:08,300
Up until now,

258
00:10:08,900 --> 00:10:10,967
even with the girlfriends
who said they liked you,

259
00:10:11,267 --> 00:10:13,000
and you tried to like them back,

260
00:10:13,567 --> 00:10:15,467
you never truly fell for them, did you?

261
00:10:17,567 --> 00:10:19,700
Well... that's true.

262
00:10:20,067 --> 00:10:21,967
Even if they already have a partner,

263
00:10:22,633 --> 00:10:24,700
the feeling of falling for someone

264
00:10:24,800 --> 00:10:26,133
is just unstoppable.

265
00:10:26,233 --> 00:10:27,233
I told you...

266
00:10:27,267 --> 00:10:29,467
An unrequited love

267
00:10:29,567 --> 00:10:30,700
is really painful,

268
00:10:31,833 --> 00:10:33,273
but even if it works out in the end,

269
00:10:33,833 --> 00:10:36,467
you'll always be haunted by guilt.

270
00:10:37,267 --> 00:10:39,967
You can never truly be happy.

271
00:10:40,567 --> 00:10:41,333
Huh?

272
00:10:41,433 --> 00:10:43,067
Sis, have you ever experienced that?

273
00:10:43,567 --> 00:10:44,567
Huh?

274
00:10:44,700 --> 00:10:45,433
Ah...

275
00:10:45,533 --> 00:10:47,933
Anyway, let's not talk about me.

276
00:10:48,033 --> 00:10:49,433
You can't just stop halfway.

277
00:10:49,533 --> 00:10:50,533
In short,

278
00:10:50,567 --> 00:10:53,900
Natsuki, don't fight
your feelings for the person you like.

279
00:10:54,900 --> 00:10:56,300
Just be honest and go for it.

280
00:10:57,333 --> 00:10:58,333
I will

281
00:10:58,400 --> 00:10:59,933
always

282
00:11:00,500 --> 00:11:01,767
be on your side.

283
00:11:03,833 --> 00:11:04,833
That's all.

284
00:11:05,867 --> 00:11:06,867
Ah.

285
00:11:21,400 --> 00:11:22,733
(Truly falling for someone.)

286
00:11:24,333 --> 00:11:27,400
If only he wasn't my sister's boyfriend...

287
00:12:02,167 --> 00:12:04,133
(Hello Shisa)
So flashy...

288
00:12:11,400 --> 00:12:12,267
Strange...

289
00:12:12,367 --> 00:12:13,600
Huh, a cold?

290
00:12:14,200 --> 00:12:15,467
It's nothing serious.

291
00:12:16,367 --> 00:12:17,933
But today's tutoring...

292
00:12:18,267 --> 00:12:19,567
Don't worry about that.

293
00:12:20,200 --> 00:12:21,933
But are you really okay?

294
00:12:22,500 --> 00:12:25,100
I went to the doctor
yesterday and got some meds.

295
00:12:25,933 --> 00:12:27,433
I should be fine in no time.

296
00:12:29,067 --> 00:12:30,067
I see.

297
00:12:30,967 --> 00:12:32,567
I'm really sorry.

298
00:12:33,067 --> 00:12:34,400
Don't.

299
00:12:34,600 --> 00:12:36,567
Just get some rest.

300
00:12:38,867 --> 00:12:39,867
Sis.

301
00:12:40,333 --> 00:12:42,700
So-chan said he caught
a cold and has a fever.

302
00:12:42,800 --> 00:12:44,233
So it really is a cold.

303
00:12:44,333 --> 00:12:44,667
Yeah.

304
00:12:44,767 --> 00:12:46,047
Sis, you should go check on him.

305
00:12:46,633 --> 00:12:47,500
Why?

306
00:12:47,600 --> 00:12:48,900
I have to go to work now.

307
00:12:49,000 --> 00:12:50,700
Huh, aren't you worried at all?

308
00:12:50,800 --> 00:12:51,833
It's just a cold, right?

309
00:12:52,133 --> 00:12:54,173
Don't they say a cold is
the root of all illnesses?

310
00:12:54,467 --> 00:12:57,033
So-chan is so healthy, he'll be fine.

311
00:12:57,133 --> 00:12:59,600
But what if he passes out?

312
00:13:00,267 --> 00:13:01,476
He might even die alone in his apartment.

313
00:13:01,500 --> 00:13:02,800
You're overreacting.

314
00:13:03,367 --> 00:13:04,267
Shoot, I gotta go.

315
00:13:04,367 --> 00:13:06,033
I'll call Sota later.

316
00:13:06,300 --> 00:13:07,300
I'm heading out.

317
00:13:08,767 --> 00:13:09,867
Take care.

318
00:13:19,700 --> 00:13:20,700
No...

319
00:13:23,633 --> 00:13:26,400
(Are you really okay?)
(It's nothing, don't worry.)

320
00:13:40,233 --> 00:13:41,500
Hasn't it gone down yet...

321
00:13:52,767 --> 00:13:55,000
How are you holding up?

322
00:13:56,400 --> 00:13:59,300
Is it really okay to ask someone
who's sick a question like that?

323
00:13:59,400 --> 00:14:01,200
What's your temperature?

324
00:14:01,800 --> 00:14:05,467
No, what's the point of asking that...

325
00:14:05,967 --> 00:14:08,233
How should I even ask?

326
00:14:13,733 --> 00:14:17,233
What kind of message should
you send to someone who's sick?

327
00:14:20,300 --> 00:14:22,567
What, "take care"?

328
00:14:23,267 --> 00:14:25,100
Ugh, what is this...

329
00:14:25,800 --> 00:14:28,467
What kind of message should
you send to someone who's sick?

330
00:14:30,967 --> 00:14:32,833
- (Kazuharu) You okay?
- (Ryo) Still alive?

331
00:14:34,167 --> 00:14:36,200
I asked the wrong people...

332
00:14:38,267 --> 00:14:39,400
Ouch.

333
00:14:39,500 --> 00:14:40,500
Hmm?

334
00:14:41,633 --> 00:14:42,667
What's going on?

335
00:14:50,700 --> 00:14:52,000
Did your fever go down?

336
00:14:54,633 --> 00:14:56,000
Na-chan...

337
00:14:59,000 --> 00:15:00,000
A reply.

338
00:15:01,067 --> 00:15:03,800
I think it should go down soon.

339
00:15:04,133 --> 00:15:05,133
Thanks.

340
00:15:05,367 --> 00:15:08,967
So that means it hasn't gone down yet?

341
00:15:12,267 --> 00:15:16,733
Why hasn't his fever gone down
even after taking the doctor's meds?

342
00:15:18,967 --> 00:15:22,033
It might mean it's not
the right medication.

343
00:15:22,400 --> 00:15:25,800
If the fever doesn't break
after three days, be careful.

344
00:15:28,533 --> 00:15:30,467
It's only the second day, huh...

345
00:15:37,967 --> 00:15:40,100
Time to eat...

346
00:15:42,633 --> 00:15:44,767
I wonder if he's eating properly...

347
00:15:54,933 --> 00:15:58,433
What happens if you don't eat
anything when you have a cold?

348
00:16:00,033 --> 00:16:04,667
If you can't keep anything down all day,
you need to be extra careful.

349
00:16:04,767 --> 00:16:07,367
If you can't even drink water,
you have to go to the hospital.

350
00:16:07,733 --> 00:16:08,733
Huh.

351
00:16:08,867 --> 00:16:11,233
If he hasn't even had
water, isn't that bad?

352
00:16:13,700 --> 00:16:15,300
Sorry for scaring you.

353
00:16:16,167 --> 00:16:19,933
Whenever I catch a cold,
Rock always sleeps next to me.

354
00:16:23,500 --> 00:16:25,867
But that guy doesn't have Rock with him.

355
00:16:41,533 --> 00:16:43,767
Would it be too annoying
to send another message...?

356
00:16:43,867 --> 00:16:46,367
But what if he really passed out...

357
00:16:46,867 --> 00:16:49,867
If he passed out, he wouldn't
be able to check his phone.

358
00:16:52,467 --> 00:16:53,467
Huh.

359
00:16:53,500 --> 00:16:54,533
If he passed out...

360
00:16:57,800 --> 00:17:00,100
(How are you doing now?)

361
00:17:00,267 --> 00:17:01,667
This should be fine.

362
00:17:09,667 --> 00:17:10,833
A reply.

363
00:17:11,733 --> 00:17:12,733
Huh.

364
00:17:16,767 --> 00:17:18,033
I should just go over.

365
00:17:50,967 --> 00:17:51,967
Huh.

366
00:17:54,900 --> 00:17:55,600
Huh.

367
00:17:55,700 --> 00:17:56,700
So-chan?

368
00:17:58,000 --> 00:18:00,133
Huh, he should be here, right?

369
00:18:01,467 --> 00:18:03,333
Huh, no way...

370
00:18:04,233 --> 00:18:05,233
So-chan!

371
00:18:06,633 --> 00:18:07,700
Answer the door!

372
00:18:10,400 --> 00:18:11,567
Na-chan?

373
00:18:12,700 --> 00:18:13,700
Huh.

374
00:18:16,400 --> 00:18:16,967
What's wrong?

375
00:18:17,067 --> 00:18:18,067
How come?

376
00:18:18,567 --> 00:18:20,067
No, that's my line.

377
00:18:21,500 --> 00:18:22,620
Weren't you running a fever?

378
00:18:22,967 --> 00:18:25,400
It broke. The meds finally kicked in.

379
00:18:27,200 --> 00:18:28,233
I see...

380
00:18:28,600 --> 00:18:30,533
And then I suddenly got hungry.

381
00:18:34,333 --> 00:18:35,333
Thank goodness.

382
00:18:35,967 --> 00:18:36,967
Don't tell me...

383
00:18:37,433 --> 00:18:39,313
Did you come because
you were worried about me?

384
00:18:43,800 --> 00:18:44,800
Na-chan...?

385
00:18:50,367 --> 00:18:51,633
Thank goodness...

386
00:18:53,500 --> 00:18:54,200
Huh, wait...

387
00:18:54,300 --> 00:18:55,300
Na-chan?

388
00:18:55,367 --> 00:18:56,367
Hold on...

389
00:18:57,233 --> 00:18:58,633
Thank goodness...

390
00:18:58,733 --> 00:19:00,067
Wh-What's wrong?

391
00:19:00,633 --> 00:19:02,167
Um, are you okay?

392
00:19:14,333 --> 00:19:15,333
So good.

393
00:19:19,133 --> 00:19:20,133
I'm glad.

394
00:19:20,533 --> 00:19:21,233
Sorry.

395
00:19:21,333 --> 00:19:23,800
It was just a cold, but I
made you worry so much.

396
00:19:25,700 --> 00:19:28,033
I was just overthinking it.

397
00:19:28,600 --> 00:19:30,633
I meant to send a smiley sticker,

398
00:19:31,067 --> 00:19:32,867
but I accidentally sent
a crying one instead.

399
00:19:33,000 --> 00:19:34,920
It made it look like I
was fishing for sympathy.

400
00:19:35,467 --> 00:19:37,300
I'm really sorry.

401
00:19:40,567 --> 00:19:41,567
But...

402
00:19:43,267 --> 00:19:46,400
I had no idea you were such a worrywart.

403
00:19:49,233 --> 00:19:50,233
Me neither...

404
00:19:52,100 --> 00:19:53,100
Huh?

405
00:19:55,267 --> 00:19:59,367
I'm not usually like this.

406
00:20:00,500 --> 00:20:03,100
Even if my sister caught a cold

407
00:20:04,633 --> 00:20:07,467
and asked me to buy her ice cream,

408
00:20:08,500 --> 00:20:11,733
I'd just find it annoying.

409
00:20:14,100 --> 00:20:15,100
But...

410
00:20:18,667 --> 00:20:22,033
the thought of you passing out, So-chan,

411
00:20:22,967 --> 00:20:26,267
or coming down with some serious illness,

412
00:20:26,600 --> 00:20:30,667
or even the thought that
you might die alone in your apartment...

413
00:20:32,333 --> 00:20:34,200
I just got so restless.

414
00:20:39,500 --> 00:20:40,667
Ah...

415
00:20:42,633 --> 00:20:43,967
So that's it...

416
00:20:45,700 --> 00:20:46,700
What's wrong?

417
00:20:48,733 --> 00:20:49,967
Could it be...

418
00:20:52,633 --> 00:20:53,867
Na-chan...?

419
00:20:56,133 --> 00:20:57,567
Is this...

420
00:20:57,667 --> 00:20:58,667
what I think it is?

421
00:21:00,633 --> 00:21:01,633
Huh?

422
00:21:04,633 --> 00:21:06,600
Could it be... I...

423
00:21:08,233 --> 00:21:11,833
actually have feelings for him?

424
00:21:12,933 --> 00:21:14,700
I've fallen for So-chan...

425
00:21:30,067 --> 00:21:31,067
Ah.

426
00:21:31,267 --> 00:21:32,367
Ah...

427
00:21:33,033 --> 00:21:36,500
Sorry... What am I even saying?

428
00:21:37,667 --> 00:21:38,700
Ah...

429
00:21:42,133 --> 00:21:44,433
Just forget what I just said.

430
00:21:45,167 --> 00:21:46,567
Pretend I was never here.

431
00:21:48,233 --> 00:21:49,500
Forget everything.

432
00:21:53,500 --> 00:21:54,500
I'm leaving.

433
00:21:54,767 --> 00:21:55,767
Na-chan!

434
00:21:57,100 --> 00:21:58,333
Wait!

435
00:22:08,033 --> 00:22:09,033
I'm sorry!

436
00:22:23,100 --> 00:22:25,667
(Incoming call: Rio)

437
00:22:25,967 --> 00:22:28,967
The person you are
calling is unavailable...

438
00:22:34,867 --> 00:22:35,867
It's this way, right?

439
00:22:43,900 --> 00:22:45,400
It should be around here, right?

440
00:22:46,467 --> 00:22:47,467
Huh?

441
00:22:48,100 --> 00:22:49,100
Wait...

442
00:22:52,633 --> 00:22:53,633
Huh?

443
00:22:54,033 --> 00:22:55,467
Why is Natsuki...

444
00:22:59,133 --> 00:23:00,133
Na-chan.

445
00:23:11,567 --> 00:23:13,100
I shouldn't...

446
00:23:15,067 --> 00:23:17,167
have ever truly fallen for someone...

447
00:23:18,333 --> 00:23:21,267
(This drama is a work of fiction)

448
00:23:21,367 --> 00:23:22,233
(Next Episode Preview)

449
00:23:22,333 --> 00:23:24,676
(Where will her closed-off heart go...) I'm never
going to fall in love or like anyone ever again.

450
00:23:24,700 --> 00:23:26,900
You like Sota, don't you?

451
00:23:27,967 --> 00:23:30,267
(Will their relationship change?)
That was just a joke...

452
00:23:30,367 --> 00:23:31,067
Did something happen?

453
00:23:31,167 --> 00:23:33,043
(A new storm brewing within the family!?)
Are you hiding something from me?

454
00:23:33,067 --> 00:23:36,133
I'm not going to fall
for my sister's boyfriend.
